+### Mastercard compliance disputes 
+
+Businesses receive Mastercard compliance disputes in certain cases when the card issuer believes the disputed transaction doesn’t conform to Mastercard’s network rules. If Mastercard compliance disputes can’t be resolved between the parties, the network resolves the dispute in exchange for a fee.
+
+If you contest a Mastercard compliance dispute, Stripe collects a 500 USD (or local equivalent) amount in addition to the applicable Stripe dispute fee or fees. This amount covers the network costs associated with resolving Mastercard compliance disputes. Stripe refunds the 500 USD network fee if you win the dispute. Learn how to respond to [Mastercard compliance disputes](https://docs.stripe.com/disputes/api/mastercard-compliance.md) using the API.
+
+> Compliance cases filed by issuers are referred to as pre-compliance disputes by Mastercard. Mastercard uses a two-stage escalation process where a pre-compliance filing can escalate to a full compliance case.
+
+### Fraudulent disputes 
 
 To help you navigate fraudulent disputes, Stripe offers Visa CE 3.0 Eligibility and liability shift.
 
-#### Visa CE 3.0 Eligibility
+#### Visa CE 3.0 Eligibility 
 
 For fraudulent disputes with the Visa 10.4 (Card absent fraud) code, Stripe automatically evaluates your transaction history to determine eligibility with [Visa Compelling Evidence 3.0](https://docs.stripe.com/disputes/best-practices.md#visa-ce-30). If your dispute is eligible, we notify you in the Dashboard and in the dispute email. In these cases, we encourage [submitting evidence](https://docs.stripe.com/disputes/responding.md#respond), because this eligibility typically translates to a significantly higher likelihood of overturning the dispute in your favor.
 
